# Cloudflare Pages reads this file at deploy time and applies these response headers.
# Everything here is static HTML/CSS with no scripts and no external requests, so the
# policy can be maximally restrictive — if a future page needs an external asset, this
# is the file that has to change first.
#
# `font-src 'self'` was added for the self-hosted Sora subset in /fonts, which the
# landing page needs for its display type. There is still no `script-src`: the site
# ships no JavaScript, and the landing page's motion is CSS scroll-driven animation,
# so `default-src 'none'` continues to block scripts outright. Keep it that way —
# every path on that page is pre-computed precisely so no script is required.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'
  # .app is on the HSTS preload list, so browsers already force HTTPS. Sending this
  # anyway covers non-preloaded aliases and keeps the header set consistent.
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
